    5. Set Pig JAR

    PIG_JAR=/usr/local/pig/pig-0.17.0-core-h2.jar

    6. Compile UDF

    javac -source 8 -target 8 \
    -cp "$PIG_JAR:$HADOOP_HOME/share/hadoop/common/*" \
    com/lab/pig/CleanDataUDF.java

    Check:

    ls -lh com/lab/pig

    7. Create JAR

    jar -cvf CleanDataUDF.jar com/lab/pig/CleanDataUDF.class
    ls -lh CleanDataUDF.jar

    8. Create Input CSV

    mkdir -p input

    cat > input/raw_logs.csv <<'EOF'
    1,Valid user session active!!!
    2,Purchase completed successfully!!!
    3,!!!
    4,
    EOF

    Check:

    cat input/raw_logs.csv

    9. Upload to HDFS

    hdfs dfs -mkdir -p /user/hadoop/pig_input
    hdfs dfs -put -f input/raw_logs.csv /user/hadoop/pig_input/
    hdfs dfs -ls /user/hadoop/pig_input
    hdfs dfs -cat /user/hadoop/pig_input/raw_logs.csv

    10. Create Pig Script

    cat > filter_script.pig <<'EOF'
    REGISTER '/home/cse/pig_lab5/CleanDataUDF.jar';

    raw_data = LOAD '/user/hadoop/pig_input/raw_logs.csv'
    USING PigStorage(',')
    AS (id:int, message:chararray);

    cleaned_tuples = FOREACH raw_data GENERATE
    id,
    com.lab.pig.CleanDataUDF(message) AS clean_msg;

    filtered_data = FILTER cleaned_tuples BY clean_msg IS NOT NULL;

    STORE filtered_data INTO '/user/hadoop/pig_output'
    USING PigStorage(',');
    EOF

    Check:

    cat filter_script.pig

    11. Remove Previous Output

    hdfs dfs -rm -r -f /user/hadoop/pig_output

    12. Run Pig

    pig -x mapreduce filter_script.pig

    Successful ending:

    Success!

    13. Check Output

    hdfs dfs -ls /user/hadoop/pig_output

    Expected:

    _SUCCESS
    part-m-00000

    14. Display Final Output

    hdfs dfs -cat /user/hadoop/pig_output/part-*

    Final:

    1,VALID USER SESSION ACTIVE
    2,PURCHASE COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY

